--- A raw DirectInput gamepad or joystick state. Axis values are device-dependent absolute values, not mouse-style deltas. Array properties use Lua indices starting at 1. Changes to this state affect engine input.
--- @class tes3directInputGamepadState
--- @field buttons number[] *Read-only*. The 32 raw button bytes, indexed from 1 to 32. Bit 0x80 indicates a held button. Button ID 0 in events and helpers corresponds to buttons[1]. Entries are writable.
--- @field povs number[] *Read-only*. The four raw POV hat values, indexed from 1 to 4. Angles are clockwise hundredths of a degree, with 0 pointing forward. A low word of 65535 indicates a centered hat (normally 4294967295). Entries are writable.
--- @field rx integer The raw absolute rx axis value. Range and availability depend on the device.
--- @field ry integer The raw absolute ry axis value. Range and availability depend on the device.
--- @field rz integer The raw absolute rz axis value. Range and availability depend on the device.
--- @field sliders number[] *Read-only*. The two raw absolute slider values, indexed from 1 to 2. Entries are writable.
--- @field x integer The raw absolute x axis value. Range and availability depend on the device.
--- @field y integer The raw absolute y axis value. Range and availability depend on the device.
--- @field z integer The raw absolute z axis value. Range and availability depend on the device.
